@startuml Audit_Logging_Flow

title Audit Logging Flow - Non-Blocking Async

participant "Workflow MS" as Workflow
participant "Audit Logger" as Logger
participant "Audit Service" as AuditService
queue "Audit Queue" as Queue
database "Audit DB" as AuditDB

== Synchronous Step Execution with Async Audit ==

Workflow -> Workflow: Execute Step\n(e.g., DECISION_CUSTOMER_EXISTS)

Workflow -> Logger: Log Audit (ASYNC)\n{\n  stepId: "...",\n  status: "...",\n  input: {...},\n  output: {...},\n  duration: ...\n}
activate Logger

note over Logger: Non-blocking call\nWorkflow continues

Logger -> Queue: Enqueue Audit Message
activate Queue
Queue --> Logger: Queued
deactivate Queue

Logger --> Workflow: Audit Queued (immediately)
deactivate Logger

Workflow -> Workflow: Continue to Next Step\n(no waiting for audit)

== Background Audit Processing ==

Queue -> AuditService: Dequeue Audit Message
activate AuditService

AuditService -> AuditService: Enrich Audit Data\n(add metadata, mask sensitive fields)

AuditService -> AuditDB: INSERT INTO audit_logs\n(auditId, workflowId, executionId,\nstepId, status, input, output,\nduration, timestamp, userId)
activate AuditDB
AuditDB --> AuditService: Inserted
deactivate AuditDB

AuditService --> Queue: Message Processed
deactivate AuditService

note over Workflow, AuditDB
  Audit logging is fully asynchronous
  and does not block workflow execution
end note

== Audit Query (Analytics/Monitoring) ==

participant "Monitoring Dashboard" as Dashboard

Dashboard -> AuditService: GET /api/v1/audit/logs\n?workflowId=CREATE_CUSTOMER_V1\n&executionId=...
activate AuditService

AuditService -> AuditDB: SELECT * FROM audit_logs\nWHERE workflowId = ?\nAND executionId = ?\nORDER BY timestamp
activate AuditDB
AuditDB --> AuditService: Audit Records
deactivate AuditDB

AuditService --> Dashboard: 200 OK\n[audit log entries]
deactivate AuditService

@enduml
